🎨 UI/UX & DaisyUI Guidelines
The "Cherry Studio" Vibe Implementation:
Sidebar (Navigation):
Use w-[64px] or w-[72px].
Background: bg-base-200 (Ensure this maps to light grey).
Active State:
Icon Container: bg-white shadow-sm rounded-xl text-[#00B96B].
Inactive State:
Icon: text-gray-500.
Forms & Inputs (Settings):
Align everything Top-Left.
Use input input-bordered input-sm from DaisyUI but styled minimally.
"Browse" buttons should use btn btn-outline btn-sm.
Layout Structure:
Always use a 3-Pane mental model:
App Sidebar (Icons)
Feature Sidebar (List/History - Optional per feature)
Main Dashboard (Content).
💻 Coding Standards
Data Fetching (React Query):
ALWAYS use useQuery for reading settings.
ALWAYS use useMutation for saving settings.
Handle isLoading and isError states gracefully (Skeleton loaders).
TypeScript:
Define strict interfaces for API responses.
Example: interface AppSettings { gemini_api_key: string; output_path: string; }.
IPC Usage:
Only use window.electron.openFileDialog() (or similar) for file picking.
Never put business logic in the Electron Main process.
📝 Code Generation Instructions
When asked to implement Settings:
Create a useSettings hook that wraps the API calls.
Create the UI that reads from this hook.
Implement the "Browse" button logic: IPC pick -> set local state -> Mutation save.
When asked for UI components:
Use Tailwind v4 syntax.
Ensure the "Green Accent" is used for primary actions and active states.
Don't use complex DaisyUI themes; stick to light mode default but override backgrounds manually to match the specific Grey/White look.